// Every card's sounds (SPEC §10.11, R655): the voices that speak its lines and the effects beside
// them. The lines' words are crates/cards/card-text.yaml's (#2498), whose export writes them to
// voice-text.json beside this file. apps/web/src/audio/voiceData.ts joins the two when the client
// loads and apps/web/scripts/gen-voice.mjs when it renders the lines. Nothing writes this file back,
// so comments and trailing commas are safe. A mistake fails the load and the tests, naming its path.
//
// Four sections, in this order:
//   voices   the voices a line can be spoken in, by name in alphabetical order. A macOS `say` voice
//            gives say, rate (90-360), pbas and pmod (0-127); backend: "sapi" is a Windows SAPI one
//            instead, with voice, rate (-50-100), semitones (-12-12) and an ffmpeg filter chain. web
//            is the browser's fallback pitch (0-2) and rate (0.1-10), gain a trim on the rendered
//            files (0-2).
//   effects  the sound effects a card can play. sfx names one of the procedural recipes in sfx.ts
//            (SFX_IDS); pitch shifts it (1 as written, 0.5 an octave down, 2 an octave up, 0.25-4),
//            gain trims it (0-2), and params passes the recipe its own options (amount, timbre,
//            mine, mythic, urgent, release). Each play varies the pitch a little.
//   cards    one entry per catalog card, in catalog order, with the card's name in a comment on
//            the line of its id. The name is for people; a test checks it against the catalog.
//   emotes   the six hero portraits' emote voices (R644), one entry per portrait id, each a voice
//            from the voices bank, which speaks the portrait's five lines in card-text.yaml
//            (greetings, wellPlayed, oops, thanks, threaten).
//
// A card's hooks are when its sounds play:
//   play     a Unit played, or put onto the field by an effect
//   attack   a Unit of yours picked up to attack (dragged, or clicked to choose its target)
//   death    a Unit destroyed
//   cast     a Spell or Field Spell cast, a Trap or Field Trap firing
//   trigger  a card whose effect summons (R1088): one of its lines plays when the runner starts the
//            `summoned` entry the card caused, picked by the client's own rng, replacing the
//            summoned card's own line for that entry
// A hook gives a voice line, { voice: "<a voice>" }, which speaks the card's line for that hook in
// card-text.yaml (a trigger's list of lines), an effect, { effect: "<an effect>" }, or both in one
// object; with both, the effect starts first. No hook here writes its words: a text or lines fails.
//
// To add a card: copy a neighbour's entry to where the catalog puts the card, change the id and the
// name comment, and give a Unit a play, an attack and a death voice (R1448), anything else a cast
// voice, writing the lines in the card's card-text.yaml entry. A new or changed line, or a line's new
// voice, has to be rendered: `pnpm --filter @jackioh/web gen:voice` on macOS, or on
// Windows (or WSL) for a SAPI voice, or a push whose commit message holds `[gen:voice]`, which renders
// both on GitHub's runners (.github/workflows/voice.yml). Effects render nothing.
{
  voices: {
    alien: { say: "Trinoids", rate: 170, pbas: 45, pmod: 20, web: { pitch: 0.5, rate: 0.9 }, gain: 1.66 },
